WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.400
We often see Elon Musk and his siblings
pictured with their mum, Maye Musk. 

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.840
Yet their relationship with their&nbsp;
father is much more complicated.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:13.280
Errol Musk is a brilliant engineer who undoubtedly&nbsp;
passed on his genes to his famous son.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:16.480
He has also been described by Elon as “evil”.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:20.320
This is the story of how he helped&nbsp;
shape the richest man in the world.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:25.440
Errol was born in Pretoria, South Africa&nbsp;
to an army sergeant father and a British&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:28.240
mother whose family is famed for their intellect.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:33.040
Errol and Maye grew up in the same neighborhood.
He fell for her supermodel looks.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:36.080
She became a well-known&nbsp;
fashion model and a dietician.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:38.800
The two dated on and off at university.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:44.080
According to Maye, Errol relentlessly pursued&nbsp;
her hand in marriage, telling Elon’s biographer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:47.200
Ashlee Vance, “He just never stopped proposing.”

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:50.640
Reminiscent of Elon’s pursuit&nbsp;
of his first wife Justine while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:53.120
they were at university together in Canada.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:57.440
Justine described to biographer Vance&nbsp;
how Elon would call her insistently,&nbsp;

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:02.000
saying, “You always knew it was Elon because&nbsp;
the phone would never stop ringing. The man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.360
does not take no for an answer. You can’t blow&nbsp;
him off. I do think of him as the Terminator. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:12.720
locks his gaze on to something and says, ‘It&nbsp;
shall be mine.’ Bit by bit, he won me over.”

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:17.920
Nine months after Errol and Maye tied&nbsp;
the knot, Elon came into the world.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:21.760
They knew their son was special from&nbsp;
a very young age as Errol told South

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:25.680
African radio station 702’s the&nbsp;
Money Show with Bruce Whitfield.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:30.720
He’s always been a very deep thinker. When he&nbsp;
was very small, for example, he would ask me:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:38.480
“Where is the whole world?”. Good question. It’s a&nbsp;
very good question, yah. I’m talking about when he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:44.720
was three or four. And these sort of questions&nbsp;
made me realize he’s a little different.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:49.840
The Musk family lived comfortably in Pretoria&nbsp;
thanks to Errol’s successful engineering business

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:52.240
and his work as a real-estate developer.

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:55.840
According to Elon, his father&nbsp;
has an extremely high IQ

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:59.280
and is a talented electrical&nbsp;
and mechanical engineer.

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:02.240
Elon benefited immensely from his father’s skill.

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:05.760
Errol used to take him and his brother&nbsp;
Kimbal to his engineering job sites

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:10.080
where they learned how to lay bricks, install&nbsp;
plumbing, and put in electrical wiring.

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:14.560
It was also Errol who introduced&nbsp;
Elon to the world of computers.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:17.280
When Elon was 11, he insisted that his dad take&nbsp;

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:20.240
him to learn how to use the new&nbsp;
computers that had just come out.

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.720
He was far too young to attend a course hosted at

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:26.000
the University of the Witwatersrand&nbsp;
in Johannesburg&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:30.000
but his dad managed to book him a spot
through his engineering connections.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.200
Errol recounted what happened&nbsp;
when Elon went to that lecture.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:38.880
Anyway, he went, and I left him there, took Kimbal&nbsp;
and I went off to get a hamburger. And came back.&nbsp;

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:44.880
It was a three-hour-long thing at Wits. And we&nbsp;
came back and everyone came out and no Elon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:52.160
And we waited and waited. And finally, went&nbsp;
into the chilly halls of Wits and found this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:58.320
sort of sloping theatre, lecture hall, rather.&nbsp;
And there was Elon with his jacket and tie off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:04.000
and his sleeves rolled up and his long grey&nbsp;
flannels, four feet high, talking to all these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:12.080
blokes from England. And when I walked up to&nbsp;
them, the one who, some professor - he didn’t even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:16.000
bother to sort of introduce himself - he&nbsp;
just said to me: ‘This boy has to have one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:20.560
of these computers.’ Anyway, we got him one of the&nbsp;
computers, and I got it at a discount, thank God.

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:24.800
With that computer, Elon&nbsp;
taught himself how to program.

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:26.880
And he was brilliant at it.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:31.680
He scored an A+ on an aptitude test for&nbsp;
programming and operating a computer when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:34.320
he briefly attended the University of Pretoria.

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:39.600
According to Maye, he had to be re-tested because&nbsp;
the university had never seen such a high score.

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:43.440
Although from the outside it may have&nbsp;
appeared Elon had a happy childhood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:48.080
he would say that it felt like&nbsp;
“misery” thanks in large part to Errol.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:52.240
Maye and Errol divorced in&nbsp;
1979 when Elon was eight.

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:55.520
She left what she described&nbsp;
as an abusive relationship.

00:03:55.520 --> 00:04:00.000
Maye struggled as a single mom. She said&nbsp;
she’d cry when one of the kids spilled milk&nbsp;

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.160
because she couldn’t buy more milk that day.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:04.640
She worked several jobs to&nbsp;
support her three children,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:09.280
bought secondhand clothes, and cooked cheap&nbsp;
and nutritious meals for them like bean stews.

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:13.760
After a couple of years, Elon felt&nbsp;
sorry that his father was living alone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:16.960
and decided to move in with him&nbsp;
in a suburb of Johannesburg.

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:19.280
It was a decision he would come to regret.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:23.840
Elon told Rolling Stone: “He&nbsp;
was such a terrible human being.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:29.600
You have no idea. My dad will have a carefully&nbsp;
thought-out plan of evil. He will plan evil.”

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:32.800
“Almost every crime you can possibly think of,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:37.520
he has done. Almost every evil thing you&nbsp;
could possibly think of, he has done.”

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:41.200
Elon never specified what&nbsp;
his father had allegedly done&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:44.160
but says he wasn’t physically violent toward him.

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:46.400
This is what we do know about Errol.

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:50.000
He once said he shot and killed&nbsp;
three people who broke into his home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:53.840
and was later cleared of all charges&nbsp;
on the grounds of self-defense.

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:56.160
He also had a child with his stepdaughter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:58.480
Jana Bezuidenhout, from another marriage.

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:02.240
He said his stepdaughter turned to him for&nbsp;
comfort after a breakup with her boyfriend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:05.280
and the child was conceived&nbsp;
“in the heat of the moment”.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:10.240
Errol has spoken out against Elon’s portrayal&nbsp;
of him, telling the UK’s Daily Mail:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:15.120
“‘Elon needs to grow up. He needs to get over&nbsp;
himself. I’m not going to hit back. I’m going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:19.600
to wait until he comes to his senses. He’s&nbsp;
having a tantrum, like a spoilt child.”

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:23.040
By the time Elon came to live&nbsp;
with him after the divorce,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:26.560
Errol claimed he was making a&nbsp;
lot of money in emerald mining.

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:31.120
Business Insider reported that Errol&nbsp;
owned half of an emerald mine in Zambia.

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:33.200
And in another Business Insider article,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:37.520
Errol said: 'We had so much money&nbsp;
we couldn't even close our safe'.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:41.440
But according to Elon, his father&nbsp;
didn’t own an emerald mine.

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:46.960
Elon tweeted that he had to work his way through&nbsp;
college, ending up with $100,000 in student debt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:50.800
and couldn’t afford a second&nbsp;
computer at his first company, Zip2.

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:56.480
He said when he emigrated from South Africa to&nbsp;
North America, he only had $2,000 in his pocket.

00:05:56.480 --> 00:05:59.360
Elon’s goal was always to&nbsp;
end up in the United States,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:02.400
the home of all the exciting&nbsp;
developments in technology.

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:06.320
To get to the States, he first went&nbsp;
to Canada, his mother’s birthplace.

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:10.720
Elon was just 17 years old when he arrived&nbsp;
in Canada, where he stayed with a cousin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:14.880
working on a farm in Saskatchewan. 
He later made his way here to Toronto,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:19.680
and also obtained passports for his mother,&nbsp;
brother, and sister to join him. They lived&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:27.040
for a time at 4000 Yonge St. in this rent-controlled apartment.
According to Maye, Elon slept on the couch.

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:29.120
His father did not wish him well.

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:32.080
In fact, Errol didn’t think his&nbsp;
son would make much of himself.

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:34.560
Elon said his father told&nbsp;
him he’d be back in South

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:37.120
Africa in three months and that he was an idiot.

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:40.400
That “idiot” went on to found and run&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:45.680
two of the most innovative and successful&nbsp;
companies in the world, Tesla and SpaceX.

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:51.280
Some have suggested that Musk’s image as the&nbsp;
savior of humanity, by accelerating the world’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:57.360
transition to sustainable energy, and by trying to&nbsp;
colonize Mars, might stem from his childhood pain.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:03.760
Rolling Stone wrote: Somewhere in this trauma&nbsp;
bond is the key to Musk’s worldview – creation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:10.000
against destruction, of being useful versus&nbsp;
harmful, of defending the world against evil.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:16.080
Does his father now believe his son will succeed&nbsp;
and go where no man or woman has gone before?

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:22.240
Is Elon going to get to Mars? He is. I don’t&nbsp;
think there’s any doubt in it whatsoever.

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:25.920
Yet it’s unlikely Elon would take&nbsp;
his father along for the ride.

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:30.960
Their relationship remains strained. 
Elon Musk is now the richest person&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:33.760
who has ever lived.
If you’d like even a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:39.520
tiny sliver of what he earns, there’s a great&nbsp;
way to invest with my sponsor Masterworks.

